  "summaries": [
    {
      "id": 240949,
      "category": "team",
      "content": "A Cross-Site Scripting (XSS) vulnerability was found on a TikTok Ads endpoint, due to a lack of appropriate HTML escaping or output encoding on the reflection of user-supplied data, which was resolved on September 7, 2022. This could have resulted in a JavaScript payload injected into the endpoint causing it to be executed within the context of the victim's browser. We thank @s3c for reporting this to our team.",
